      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MODERN GIRL (6) missed narrowly fresh before leading all the way for a dominant fashion, bolting in by 4.5L at Bunbury. She jumped a $1.70 favourite there and looks right up to this level - if not better. Can speed to the front again and be very tough to run down. BRINSON (5) jumped out well but failed in her only run last campaign at Wodonga. Now lines up for the Fiore stable with Pike on board following a sharp trial in readiness for this. Ticks plenty of boxes and can make a statement. DON'T WINK (2) missed by 0.9L on resumption at this track and trip and there's a winner already out of that event. O'Donnell remains in the irons and with that run under the belt, she can go one better. G'DAY BLOKE (7) was solid on resumption without a trial under his belt. He's a second-up winner in the past and he can feature in the finish. HEZ GOT THE SAFE (1) can feature with the aid of an inside draw.",
